@@ -128,3 +128,17 @@ An operator wants to load a Laguna model (safetensors format) that has no GGUF r
 - llama.cpp blocking C FFI calls are wrapped with `tokio::task::spawn_blocking`; callers treat the engine as fully async.
 - The Nix flake build gains CUDA toolkit inputs for the daemon derivation; non-CUDA builds remain possible by omitting the `cuda` feature.
 - The NixOS module lives at `flake/nixosModules/agentix.nix` as a flake-parts module (wrapper + NixOS content inline; `recursiveImports` picks it up automatically). GPU architecture selection is driven by `nixpkgs.config.cudaCapabilities`; the module emits a `config.warnings` entry when that option is unset so operators know inference will be CPU-only.
+
+## Task 2 addendum: Explicit routing fallback
+
+Callers may supply a `RouteTarget` for unrecognized model names through
+`Router::route_with_default(&self, model: &str, default: RouteTarget) -> RouteTarget`.
+Every recognized rule retains its priority and case-insensitive behavior. Existing
+`route()` calls continue to default to Local. The daemon chat completion caller
+uses its configured fallback (`AGENTIX_DEFAULT_ROUTE`: local, anthropic, openai,
+openrouter; missing or unrecognized values select local).
+
+Acceptance: recognized names ignore a conflicting fallback, unknown names use
+each explicitly supplied target, and the existing Local fallback remains intact.
+Validate with `nix develop --command cargo test -p agentix-router` and
+`nix develop --command cargo check --workspace`.
